# Trivy ignore file — scoped exceptions only, each with its reason written here.
#
# This file exists so that one known, documented, upstream-unfixed finding does not either hide
# behind a blanket `ignore-unfixed` or hold the whole pipeline red. Anything NOT listed here
# still fails the build at CRITICAL/HIGH.

# CVE-2026-76642 — util-linux (bsdutils, libblkid1, liblastlog2-2): unprivileged mount-helper
#   exit-status check allows privilege escalation via X-mount.idmap / X-mount.owner hooks.
# CVE-2026-78408 — util-linux: nsenter --join-cgroup leaks root.
# CVE-2026-78409 — util-linux: X-mount.subdir detached-tree handling.
# CVE-2026-78410 — util-linux: restricted bind mounts do not pin the source.
#
#   WHY IGNORED: the image is based on python:3.12-slim = Debian trixie. Debian's security
#   tracker marks trixie VULNERABLE with no fix for these four (util-linux is marked <no-dsa>,
#   classified minor) and the fixes exist only in forky/sid (2.42.4-1). Docker Hub publishes no
#   forky variant of the `python` image, so there is no patched base to move to. The Dockerfile
#   now runs `apt-get upgrade`, which clears the four CVEs that DO have trixie fixes
#   (CVE-2025-69720, CVE-2026-16742, CVE-2026-54369, CVE-2026-9538); these four remain because
#   Debian has released nothing for them yet.
#
#   This is tracked in docs/implementation/HANDOFF.md. Re-check when trixie gets a DSA or a
#   forky-based Python image is published — then delete the corresponding entries.
CVE-2026-76642
CVE-2026-78408
CVE-2026-78409
CVE-2026-78410
